      "role": "user",
      "content": "Right, I see what you mean. But if you were actually running this through the scoring engine to generate a specific risk rating, how would the engine actually handle that difference in neighborhood? Like, if you had to make a call on which one is a \"safer\" bet for a high-limit loan, would the urban vs suburban distinction actually tip the scale in one direction?",
